<title>USA: Meadowbrook stock plunges on sharply lower profits.</title>
<headline>Meadowbrook stock plunges on sharply lower profits.</headline>
<dateline>SOUTHFIELD, Mich.</dateline>
<text>
<p>The stock of Meadowbrook Insurance Group Inc. lost nearly 40 percent of its value Wednesday after the insurance company reported sharply lower earnings due to higher than expected claims.</p>
<p>Meadowbrook plunged $10.75 to $15.625 on the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>The company announced third quarter earnings of $492,000 or 5 cents a share compared with year-ago earnings of $3.4 million or 38 cents a share.</p>
<p>Its revenues were flat at $27.8 million.</p>
